This tool assists in the random selection of quadrats to use as sample units in vegetation sampling. It takes an area of interest and populates it with a specified number of quadrats of a specified size, and makes sure they don't overlap. To run the tool your workspace must be set to the data folder included with the tool, run the cell in the included notebook with the correct path for your computer to accomplish this. Next, select your area of interest, quadrat count, and quadrat size, as well as the name for the feature that is being created. Hit run. The tool should generate a polygon for your aoi as well as the specified number of polygons. If you get an error or the tool runs but never completes, try either reducing the number of quadrats or their size. The tool will not work if the aoi is not big enough for the amount of quadrats chosen.
